## What I checked

- **Sources:** I reopened all 27 sources behind the final claims. 25 were refetched live; Country Now and USA Today block scripted requests, so I read those in Internet Archive captures. Every quoted string in the body traces to its source with the right speaker, date and context.
- **Video quotes:** I refetched the caption tracks and ran a third machine transcription on nine segments. Everything agrees except one word (see finding 1). No person has listened to any audio.
- **Currency:** searches today found no reply from her on the song comparisons, no management statement and no interview after August, so the "as of October 11" statements hold.
- **Jury decisions:** all 48 are accepted, including the one rejection (the public-health backstory, left out on sensitivity grounds). All 23 protected passages are preserved, six of them reworded to remove unsupported detail.
- **Re-ranked rival:** the edit moved the closest rival from Type 7 to Type 6. That does not need a fresh jury. The leading type is unchanged, Six was already in the reviewed live set, and four of the six jurors asked for the change.
- **Open-case eligibility:** confirmed. She is 24, her breakout was January to March 2026, and my own searches found no pre-2026 interviews or pre-fame testimony.

